title: Claude Code's price per token differs by model, and the transcripts let it be reproduced to the cent.
pid: c0ed40b3-0f80-4ad6-a02b-b9a5b460ba16
body: |2-
  Dollars per million tokens, as Claude Code applies them, recovered by
  fitting its 'cost-state' records: Fable 5.2 $8 in, $40 out; Opus 5.5
  $4 and $20; Sonnet 5.5 $2 and $10; Haiku 5.5 $0.10 and $0.50. A cache
  read costs a twentieth of input (a fortieth for Fable, a tenth for
  Haiku); a cache write 1.25 times input if kept five minutes, twice if
  kept an hour (assumed for Sonnet and Haiku, not yet seen keeping one),
  and each request's usage says which. So the pacer's Top, on Fable, costs
  twice what an Opus specialist costs per token. These are list prices;
  how the subscription's limits weigh tokens is not published, so a
  dollar figure measures the subscription only as far as they follow list prices.
